Text after an atomic inline can wrap away from it, except when it
starts with a character of the GL (other than U+00A0), WJ, or ZWJ line
breaking class. Blink does the same: Its InlineItemsBuilder puts U+FFFC
OBJECT REPLACEMENT CHARACTER in the text for each atomic inline, and
UAX #14 allows a break on either side of that character, except where
one of those classes is next to it.
